{"id":"reuel","name":"Reuel","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:reuel"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Reuel","text":"Friend of God. (1.) A son of Esau and Bashemath (Gen. 36:4, 10; 1 Chr. 1:35). (2.) “The priest of Midian,” Moses’ father-in-law (Ex. 2:18)=Raguel (Num. 10:29). If he be identified with Jethro (q.v.), then this may be regarded as his proper name, and Jether or Jethro (i.e., “excellency”) as his official title. (3.) Num. 2:14, called also Deuel (1:14; 7:42)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H7467","lemma":"רְעוּאֵל","xlit":"Rᵉʻûwʼêl","gloss":"Reuel, the name of Moses' father-in-law, also of an Edom","kjv":"Raguel, Reuel","count":9,"share":0.69},{"strong":"H460","lemma":"אֶלְיָסָף","xlit":"ʼElyâçâph","gloss":"Eljasaph, the name of two Israelites","kjv":"Eliasaph","count":5,"share":0.38},{"strong":"H1845","lemma":"דְּעוּאֵל","xlit":"Dᵉʻûwʼêl","gloss":"Deuel, an Israelite","kjv":"Deuel","count":4,"share":0.31},{"strong":"H1315","lemma":"בׇּשְׂמַת","xlit":"Bosmath","gloss":"Bosmath, the name of a wife of Esau, and of a daughter o","kjv":"Bashemath, Basmath","count":4,"share":0.31},{"strong":"H6215","lemma":"עֵשָׂו","xlit":"ʻÊsâv","gloss":"Esav, a son of Isaac, including his posterity","kjv":"Esau","count":5,"share":0.38},{"strong":"H4199","lemma":"מִזָּה","xlit":"Mizzâh","gloss":"Mizzah, an Edomite","kjv":"Mizzah","count":3,"share":0.23}],"verses":["Gen.36.4","Gen.36.10","Gen.36.13","Gen.36.17","Exod.2.18","Num.2.14","1Chr.1.35","1Chr.1.37","1Chr.9.8","Num.1.14","Num.7.42","Num.7.47","Num.10.20"],"related":[{"id":"jethro","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"eliasaph","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.357,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"deuel","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.308,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"bashemath","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.267,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"mizzah","type":"cooccur","s